'''Sicarus Incarnon Genesis''' is an item that is used to add [[Incarnon]] upgrades to the {{Weapon|Sicarus}} or {{Weapon|Sicarus Prime}}.

==Acquisition==
*Upon completion of [[The Duviri Paradox]] and [[Angels of the Zariman]], and unlocking [[The Steel Path]], players can earn {{Resource|Sicarus Incarnon Genesis}} from [[The Circuit]]'s Steel Path to place on their Sicarus with the help of [[Cavalero]] in the [[Chrysalith]]. This [[Incarnon Genesis]] form grants it evolutions to a transformation and newfound strength.
*Purchased from Cavalero for {{pc|120}}, complete with the resources used in its installation. This purchase can only be made '''once'''.

==Incarnon Genesis==

===Evolutions===
*Installing the Sicarus Incarnon Genesis requires 20 {{Resource|Pathos Clamp|Pathos Clamps}}, 100 {{Resource|Nacreous Pebble}}, and 150 {{Resource|Aggristone}}.
*When installed, the first Evolution tier is unlocked. The following Evolution tiers, their requirements for unlocking them, and their related perks, are shown below;
**Each challenge additionally grants 5,000 [[affinity]] to the weapon, affected by [[Affinity Booster]]s.

====Evolution I====
*Weakpoint hits charge Incarnon Transmutation; Alt Fire transmutes. Switching back will expend any remaining charge.
*Bullets [[ricochet]].
**Shots ricochet to '''1''' nearby enemy within '''6''' meters of the main target and any subsequent targets struck by punch through. 
**Ricochets '''can''' hit weakpoints, but not reliably.
*Base damage, base [[Critical Chance]], and base [[Critical Multiplier]] are increased. {{Weapon|Sicarus}} also gains increased base [[Status Chance]].
*Mode switching is '''not''' instantaneous and has an animation equal to the weapon's [[reload speed]].
*Incarnon Form is activated by filling the Incarnon Transmutation gauge that appears under the reticle by achieving [[Enemy Body Parts|weakpoint hits]] and then pressing the [[Alternate Fire]] button. '''12''' weakpoints (or '''4''' bursts) will completely fill the gauge. A full gauge is not required to activate Incarnon Form.
**Charges do '''not''' generate on the backpacks of most [[MOA]] variants, or vulnerability spots generated by {{A|Sonar}} or {{M|Detect Vulnerability}} in places other than actual weakpoints.
**Weakpoints on corpses or [[Invulnerable]] targets do '''not''' build charges.
**Individual [[Multishot]] bullets can build charges.
*Instead of drawing ammunition from its reserves, the Sicarus's Incarnon Form uses a separate "magazine" with each charge producing '''10''' rounds to a maximum of '''120'''. Once all ammunition is expended, the Sicarus reverts to its normal form.
**Incarnon Form's magazine is '''not''' affected by mods.
**Incarnon Form is '''not''' affected by [[Ammo Efficiency]] (such as {{A|Energized Munitions}}).
**Charges and Incarnon Form persists through all activities, such as holstering, [[bleedout]], or being [[disarm]]ed. However, charges and Incarnon Form are removed upon [[death]].
*Swapping to and from Incarnon Form will fully reload the normal form's magazine.

====Evolution II====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Complete a solo mission with this weapon equipped.
*Perk 1: '''Feigned Retreat:'''
**Increase Base Damage by '''+50''' (Sicarus) / '''+40''' (Prime)
**'''+40%''' Damage to enemies below half Health
***Bonus damage is additive with mods such as {{M|Hornet Strike}}, but does not take into account the Base Damage increase from this perk.
*Perk 2: '''King's Gambit:'''
**Increase Base Damage by '''+50''' (Sicarus) / '''+40''' (Prime)
**'''x0''' [[Critical Chance]] on Bodyshots, '''+150%''' Critical Chance on Weakpoint Hits
***Bodyshot modifier is multiplicative with all sources of Critical Chance, effectively making non-headshot critical hits impossible.
****{{WF|Citrine}}'s {{A|Crystallize}} is an exception to this.
***Weakpoint modifier is additive with mods such as {{M|Pistol Gambit}}
*The increased Base Damage from these perks are not taken into account for the damage bonus of {{M|Galvanized Shot}}.
====Evolution III====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Kill '''100''' enemies with this weapon's Incarnon Form.
*Perk 1: '''Void's Guidance:'''
**'''+40%''' [[Accuracy]]
**'''-40%''' Weapon [[Recoil]]
*Perk 2: '''Rapid Reinforcement:'''
**'''+50%''' [[Reload Speed]]
*Perk 3: '''Extended Volley:'''
**Increase Base [[Magazine Capacity]] by '''+9''' (Sicarus) / '''+12''' (Prime)

====Evolution IV====
*''Unlock Challenge:'' Get '''40''' weakpoint hits with this weapon in Incarnon form in a single mission.
*Perk 1: '''Commodore's Fortune:'''
**Increase Base [[Critical Chance]] by '''+18%''' (Sicarus) / '''14%''' (Prime)
*Perk 2: '''Survivor's Edge:'''
**Increase Base [[Critical Chance]] by '''12%''' (Sicarus) / '''+9%''' (Prime)
**Increase Base [[Status Chance]] to '''12%''' (Sicarus) / '''+9%''' (Prime)
*Perk 3: '''Wiseman's Regard:'''
**Increase Base [[Status Chance]] by '''30%''' of current [[Critical Chance]], up to '''40%'''
***Maximum Base Status Chance increase is gained at '''134%''' Critical Chance, achievable with '''+734%''' (Sicarus) / '''+434%''' (Prime) modded Critical Chance, or '''+567%''' (Sicarus) / '''+345%''' (Prime) in Incarnon Form.
***Incarnon Form Status Chance is displayed in the [[Arsenal]] screen as if using the normal form's Critical Chance, but will properly use its' own Critical chance while in-mission.
***In addition to regular Critical Chance mods, it is also affected by both parts of {{M|Galvanized Crosshairs}} while aiming, {{Arcane|Secondary Outburst}}, {{Arcane|Cascadia Overcharge}}, {{Arcane|Arcane Avenger}}, {{WF|Yareli}}'s Passive, {{WF|Zephyr}}'s Passive, {{A|Covenant}}'s baseline Critical Chance bonus but ''not'' the 4x multiplier on headshots, and {{M|Cat's Eye}}.
***'''Not''' affected by the '''King's Gambit''' Evolution II perk, {{Arcane|Cascadia Accuracy}}, {{A|Crystallize}}, or {{M|Shadow Haze}}.

